  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Area-Based-Allocation: Reactivation of primary paediatric services for the population of South Darfur</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtThe primary objective of this initiative is to re-open the EMERGENCY paediatric clinic in order to resume and ensure continuity ofltbrgtpaediatric healthcare services, aiming to decrease the elevated rates of morbidity and mortality in the South Darfur region. This isltbrgtachieved by offering essential healthcare services that are in short supply to internally displaced persons (IDPs) and host communities inltbrgtNyala and its surroundings.ltbrgtThe Action will take place in the premises of the Nyala Paediatric Centre, EMERGENCY&#x2019;s own paediatric hospital located in the area ofltbrgtAl Nahda in Nyala Shimal (Nyala North).ltbrgtFollowing the assault on the Nyala Paediatric Centre on 25 October 2023 by a phalanx of Rapid Support Forces (RSF) and itsltbrgtsubsequent looting, EMERGENCY was forced to interrupt its activities. As a consequence, Output 1 revolves around the rehabilitation ofltbrgtthe clinic. The restoration efforts will primarily target the purchase of essential equipment required to resume basic and urgent activities,ltbrgtwith the ultimate goal of ensuring Output 2 &#x2013; namely by providing continuity of outpatient services (OPD) in order to swiftly reinstate lifesavingltbrgtand free-of-charge healthcare services for the paediatric population of South Darfur. Besides, Output 3 is closely intertwined,ltbrgtaiming to secure the continuity of the INR follow-up service for individuals who have undergone life-saving therapy following cardiacltbrgtsurgery for heart valve replacement. This comprehensive approach seeks to address both the immediate and ongoing healthcare needsltbrgtof the affected population.ltbrgtThe primary focus of this initiative is children aged 0-14. However, the positive impact extends to the families of the patients receivingltbrgthigh quality and free-of-charge treatment at the EMERGENCY Paediatric Centre. By relieving the financial burden associated withltbrgtmedical care, the most economically disadvantaged sections of the population will experience significant benefits.ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
